# Question folder contract

Every `questions/<slug>/` folder must include:

- `README.md` — five interview steps plus **What we implemented**; step 2 has one heading per functional requirement (`17-high-level-by-requirement.mdc`); include options/tradeoffs taught in the session, not only the chosen path
- `FAQ.md` — Q&A in the five steps, plus **Session questions** (user questions from the end of practice and the answers)
- `FLOW.md` — one chart per feature, client to load balancer to gateway to the named service to the named database (`19-final-design-flow.mdc`)
- `final-design-flow.md` — end picture: request paths, each service and its job, each database type and schema (`19-final-design-flow.mdc`)
- `high-level-design-comparision.md` — study comparison of the important features across Hello Interview, Alex Xu, this session, and production (`18-high-level-design-comparison.mdc`)
- `COMPONENTS.md` — each important piece: definition + role in *this* design
- `docker-compose.yml` — local mocked components (app UI + API, database, extras)
- `scripts/setup.sh` — activate `system-design-interview` venv, then bring frontend, backend, and data stores up
- `scripts/stop.sh` — `docker compose down` (no `-v`); run when the question session ends
- `scripts/run-scenarios.sh` — integration tests against running containers
- `scripts/run-functional.sh` — functional tests of user-visible flows
- `src/` — backend (and static frontend unless `frontend/` is separate)
- `tests/` — integration/functional helpers

Status in README: **Stub** (placeholders), **Designed** (docs filled, no running system), or **Implemented** (setup + integration + functional tests work). Re-practice updates the same folder; do not freeze Implemented docs/code.

Slug is kebab-case. Overlapping names from Hello Interview and Alex Xu share one folder.
